@h1 Comments h1@

A comment is a note to yourself that no reader ever sees — a TODO, a source to
check, an editorial aside.

@@@pre
~ verify this date before publishing
The lighthouse was automated in 1998.
pre@@@

A line that starts with @@@code ~ code@@@ followed by a space is a comment. It
vanishes from every output — HTML, Markdown, and PDF alike.

@h2 One caution h2@

Don't put a comment as the very @em first em@ line inside a node's body without
a blank line after it — under the covers it can pull the following block into
the wrong place. A blank line right after the comment always avoids it:

@@@pre
@section

  ~ this comment is safe — note the blank line above and below

  @h2 A heading that stays a heading h2@
section@
pre@@@
